WEBVTT

1
00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.958
MY BELOVED DEMON

2
00:00:44.085 --> 00:00:45.462
Do as you like.

3
00:00:48.506 --> 00:00:50.049
Because it's better for me.

4
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.468
They are all dead.

5
00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.094
Ms. Chu,

6
00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:54.512
mom and dad

7
00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.348
Everyone I loved in my life is dead.

8
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.310
And you will die too...

9
00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.230
through me

10
00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:06.900
I don't care.

11
00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:37.907
your wound

12
00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.450
It cannot be wetted.

13
00:02:58.261 --> 00:02:59.095
You…

14
00:03:00.263 --> 00:03:01.347
Your strength...

15
00:03:03.474 --> 00:03:04.559
My powers...

16
00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:07.395
returned

17
00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:09.058
EPISODE 9
THE UNCOVERED TRUTH

18
00:05:13.771 --> 00:05:15.315
{\an8}That's why...

19
00:05:18.026 --> 00:05:20.153
{\an8}do people deliberately do stupid things?

20
00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:36.085
{\an8}What happened?

21
00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.295
{\an8}When did you wake up?

22
00:05:38.588 --> 00:05:39.547
{\an8}It's been a long time.

23
00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.716
{\an8}Did I snore?

24
00:05:41.799 --> 00:05:43.926
- I wouldn't be against the worst.
- Did I snore?

25
00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.179
- No.
- Exactly?

26
00:05:46.262 --> 00:05:48.848
Yes. So let me see your face.

27
00:05:48.931 --> 00:05:49.766
No.

28
00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:51.267
Why not?

29
00:05:52.101 --> 00:05:55.104
I don't know. I feel a little embarrassed.

30
00:05:56.147 --> 00:05:57.648
Let's go somewhere. I'm hungry

31
00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.319
I thought you had enough
cups of hand-brewed coffee.

32
00:06:01.402 --> 00:06:03.780
I know Maybe it's because
that I am almost human now.

33
00:06:07.575 --> 00:06:09.327
You didn't book the whole restaurant today.

34
00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:10.661
i realized

35
00:06:10.745 --> 00:06:13.831
which might not be such a bad idea
to eat among people.

36
00:06:13.915 --> 00:06:15.541
When there are so many of them around

37
00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:17.001
it's cute and lively.

38
00:06:21.172 --> 00:06:22.381
One double order.

39
00:06:22.965 --> 00:06:26.052
I'm afraid it's only available for Christmas, sir.

40
00:06:27.637 --> 00:06:30.014
But that is the reason we are here.

41
00:06:30.598 --> 00:06:32.558
Can it not be considered
what is christmas today

42
00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:35.186
To mark
my stay among people.

43
00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.522
No ingredients sir.

44
00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:38.856
Exactly?

45
00:06:41.359 --> 00:06:43.861
Then let's find another institution,
where paired dishes are served.

46
00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:45.488
Just two of these, please.

47
00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:46.906
Yes, ma'am.

48
00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:52.078
Isn't this discrimination against demons?

49
00:06:52.161 --> 00:06:53.913
Why paired dishes
only on Jesus' birthday?

50
00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:56.958
Let's go back to Christmas
and let's celebrate with your favorite cake.

51
00:06:57.041 --> 00:07:00.294
You tell the demon
celebrate the birth of Jesus?

52
00:07:00.378 --> 00:07:01.712
So you don't want to?

53
00:07:01.796 --> 00:07:02.797
No, I didn't say that.

54
00:07:03.714 --> 00:07:07.343
Not that I don't want to. Just said so.

55
00:07:08.719 --> 00:07:12.431
But why is everyone so excited about Christmas?

56
00:07:12.515 --> 00:07:15.351
For some reason, Christmas brings joyous excitement.

57
00:07:16.144 --> 00:07:17.395
It's like becoming a child again.

58
00:07:17.478 --> 00:07:19.313
now i understand

59
00:07:19.397 --> 00:07:22.775
why is everyone so noisy
and intemperate at Christmas.

60
00:07:23.818 --> 00:07:26.028
i will try my best
as my name suggests.

61
00:07:26.904 --> 00:07:29.365
I don't want to brag

62
00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:32.452
but somehow I was wooed by a chaebol.

63
00:07:33.035 --> 00:07:37.748
The famous heiress
fell in love with me at first sight

64
00:07:38.332 --> 00:07:40.543
and chased
for us to register the marriage.

65
00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:44.422
But I told her:
"I refuse to be a chaebol dog.

66
00:07:44.505 --> 00:07:47.300
I will be the hunting dog of the public."

67
00:07:47.383 --> 00:07:51.262
I refused her so coldly and decisively.

68
00:07:53.514 --> 00:07:54.599
A hunting dog?

69
00:07:54.682 --> 00:07:57.143
Is that why you're trying to sniff everything out?

70
00:08:00.897 --> 00:08:02.773
Maybe we will continue elsewhere?

71
00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.195
Yes, love at first sight.

72
00:08:07.278 --> 00:08:09.197
- Give me the wrist.
- Why?

73
00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.492
To teach him
not to talk about you.

74
00:08:12.575 --> 00:08:14.494
He wants to be a hunting dog,

75
00:08:14.577 --> 00:08:16.329
then I can give him a nose…

76
00:08:16.412 --> 00:08:17.580
leave it

77
00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:20.124
That's what I suggested
to register the marriage and refused.

78
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:22.293
Why do you side with that scoundrel?

79
00:08:22.376 --> 00:08:24.670
How annoying.

80
00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.049
By the way, did I tell you?

81
00:08:28.132 --> 00:08:28.966
What did she tell me?

82
00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.427
I don't go to work now.
The anniversary of the company's foundation.

83
00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:32.428
Really?

84
00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:41.270
What is going on anyway?

85
00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:44.774
Why isn't Director Jeon happy,
that To To Hee resigned?

86
00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.776
Shouldn't he be glad she's safe?

87
00:08:47.485 --> 00:08:48.528
God

88
00:08:49.904 --> 00:08:51.197
Is he still sleeping?

89
00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.742
It's great not having to go to work.

90
00:08:55.243 --> 00:08:57.453
I thought you liked going to work.

91
00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.580
I thought so too

92
00:08:59.664 --> 00:09:01.624
until she fell in love with a demon.

93
00:09:03.125 --> 00:09:06.879
So what do people usually do on a date?

94
00:09:06.963 --> 00:09:09.882
They usually eat and drink coffee.

95
00:09:10.508 --> 00:09:11.384
And that's all.

96
00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:13.302
How insignificant.

97
00:09:14.762 --> 00:09:15.972
Even if with me?

98
00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:22.728
What is it?

99
00:09:22.812 --> 00:09:24.564
<i>I'm at the door, Director Jon.</i>

100
00:09:24.647 --> 00:09:26.232
Open it.

101
00:09:26.315 --> 00:09:27.400
I'm not at home now.

102
00:09:27.483 --> 00:09:28.484
So where are you?

103
00:09:28.568 --> 00:09:30.194
We are near the Khan River.

104
00:09:30.278 --> 00:09:32.238
That's right. We are on a date.

105
00:09:32.321 --> 00:09:34.323
<i>- In your condition?</i>
- I have completely recovered.

106
00:09:37.159 --> 00:09:38.411
CALL COMPLETED
DIRECTOR CHON

107
00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.248
What did I miss?

108
00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:44.625
I am interested in this.

109
00:09:44.709 --> 00:09:47.003
What kind of insignificant things are these?

110
00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:48.296
- So?
- Yes.

111
00:09:48.879 --> 00:09:50.172
These are bikes for couples.

112
00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:51.841
Steam…

113
00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.134
For couples?

114
00:09:53.217 --> 00:09:54.510
Let's try to ride!

115
00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:56.095
He is so insignificant.

116
00:09:56.178 --> 00:09:57.722
I love insignificant things.

117
00:09:57.805 --> 00:09:58.681
Come on.

118
00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:00.349
- What?
- Numo.

119
00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:02.310
Where are we going?

120
00:10:02.393 --> 00:10:04.228
- Let's go get such a bike.
- But...

121
00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:17.408
Why are you sitting in the front?

122
00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:20.161
Wait, look!

123
00:10:20.244 --> 00:10:22.038
- What?
- He is there!

124
00:10:23.998 --> 00:10:26.250
Let's try that little thing.

125
00:10:26.334 --> 00:10:28.419
Is everything for couples now?

126
00:10:28.502 --> 00:10:29.503
Come on?

127
00:10:29.587 --> 00:10:31.422
- Of course, let's go.
- Forward.

128
00:10:31.505 --> 00:10:32.465
- That's right.
- Good.

129
00:10:32.548 --> 00:10:34.467
- Forward.
- I raise my legs.

130
00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:36.844
That's it.

131
00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:43.643
- Higher!
- Higher!

132
00:10:43.726 --> 00:10:45.311
- I say above!
- Up!

133
00:10:45.895 --> 00:10:47.229
What could it be?

134
00:10:48.689 --> 00:10:51.525
- Higher!
- What would be the most effective way

135
00:10:51.609 --> 00:10:54.570
fool us while we relax?

136
00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:56.781
- Higher!
- Maybe...

137
00:10:56.864 --> 00:10:58.574
- It can't be.
- Even higher!

138
00:10:59.158 --> 00:11:00.451
Then what about…

139
00:11:00.534 --> 00:11:01.702
No, and not that.

140
00:11:01.786 --> 00:11:03.788
My head is splitting, damn it.

141
00:11:03.871 --> 00:11:07.333
I remember that I had a high IQ,
but did I drink too much?

142
00:11:07.416 --> 00:11:09.043
It looks like all the brain cells have died.

143
00:11:10.336 --> 00:11:11.337
Sneeze.

144
00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.923
I would rather do than think.

145
00:11:16.759 --> 00:11:18.386
- How cute.
- I like it here.

146
00:11:18.469 --> 00:11:20.846
Artificial landscapes are the most beautiful.

147
00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.057
Isn't it usually the other way around?

148
00:11:24.392 --> 00:11:27.812
I prefer
created by people, not by God.

149
00:11:27.895 --> 00:11:30.481
That's why I'm more of a collector,
than a traveler.

150
00:11:30.564 --> 00:11:31.816
Don't you like God?

151
00:11:32.733 --> 00:11:34.735
Does anyone like their boss?

152
00:11:37.738 --> 00:11:39.615
Although I have never met God personally,

153
00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:41.075
unable to bind.

154
00:11:41.617 --> 00:11:44.537
And it didn't help that I'm 200 years old
watched the decline of the world.

155
00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.040
I wonder what your life was like

156
00:11:48.707 --> 00:11:51.043
the past 200 years.

157
00:11:51.669 --> 00:11:54.964
An insignificant person
will never understand the experience of a demon.

158
00:11:57.049 --> 00:11:58.634
I'm not trying to understand you.

159
00:11:59.593 --> 00:12:02.763
I'm just trying
accept you as you are.

160
00:12:06.016 --> 00:12:09.353
It seems that the demons were the guardians of mankind.

161
00:12:10.855 --> 00:12:11.689
Really?

162
00:12:12.273 --> 00:12:13.232
"Give me."

163
00:12:13.858 --> 00:12:16.652
In ancient Greek it means
"to share the same fate."

164
00:12:16.735 --> 00:12:18.279
The word "demon" comes from him.

165
00:12:18.362 --> 00:12:20.156
"To share the same fate."

166
00:12:24.326 --> 00:12:26.120
your truth
that we share the same fate.

167
00:12:29.957 --> 00:12:32.001
Then how did demons become bad?

168
00:12:33.627 --> 00:12:36.797
Let's say I succumbed to life's difficulties.

169
00:12:37.548 --> 00:12:40.259
People turn to the dark side
after several years of work.

170
00:12:40.342 --> 00:12:42.011
I had to do it for 200 years.

171
00:12:43.637 --> 00:12:45.097
Looks like you're not that bad.

172
00:12:49.685 --> 00:12:53.022
So you came back
to its original being.

173
00:13:02.823 --> 00:13:04.408
You are my keeper.

174
00:13:33.854 --> 00:13:34.939
Come on.

175
00:13:35.523 --> 00:13:36.357
{\an8}Okay.

176
00:13:40.945 --> 00:13:44.490
Customer number 82, your paired drinks

177
00:13:44.573 --> 00:13:46.825
and a gift soft toy are ready.

178
00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:49.245
Thank you.

179
00:13:49.328 --> 00:13:51.288
No, I'm thanking you.

180
00:14:07.346 --> 00:14:08.389
It's starting to seem

181
00:14:09.265 --> 00:14:12.851
that people are insignificant and at the same time charming.

182
00:14:13.602 --> 00:14:16.272
It's like I took a kitten

183
00:14:16.897 --> 00:14:19.650
and began to care
about all the homeless cats in the world.

184
00:14:20.234 --> 00:14:23.988
Who knew attachment was contagious?

185
00:14:24.572 --> 00:14:27.908
You're comparing me to a cat now
and not with a weasel beetle?

186
00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.204
what do you want honey

187
00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.540
Same as you dear.

188
00:14:38.669 --> 00:14:40.754
Whatever you want to call a kitten,
maybe call "dear"?

189
00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:42.381
No.

190
00:14:42.464 --> 00:14:44.049
can you call me man

191
00:14:45.467 --> 00:14:46.468
You must be crazy.

192
00:14:47.052 --> 00:14:48.387
What are you talking about?

193
00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:49.305
I am your husband.

194
00:14:54.393 --> 00:14:56.103
- Let the kitten be better.
- No.

195
00:14:59.106 --> 00:15:00.524
Look how beautiful it is.

196
00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:02.401
Yes.

197
00:15:18.334 --> 00:15:20.711
Seriously, she's forever noticing everything.

198
00:15:22.087 --> 00:15:23.297
God

199
00:15:29.094 --> 00:15:30.429
beautiful

200
00:15:31.513 --> 00:15:32.598
And this one is beautiful.

201
00:15:32.681 --> 00:15:34.600
All photos are flawless.

202
00:15:35.309 --> 00:15:36.727
They are so photogenic.

203
00:15:39.605 --> 00:15:41.857
God, what am I even doing?

204
00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:43.984
I am not their photographer.

205
00:15:45.152 --> 00:15:46.904
Pull yourself together, No Soo An.

206
00:15:46.987 --> 00:15:49.323
You came to dig up the truth.

207
00:15:50.741 --> 00:15:53.327
She can fool everyone, but not me.

208
00:15:54.411 --> 00:15:58.874
To To Hee, time for you
show its true ugly face.

209
00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.676
Why did you refuse to go?
on that little ferry?

210
00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:11.428
Then. We have a lot of time.

211
00:16:11.512 --> 00:16:12.680
When then?

212
00:16:12.763 --> 00:16:13.973
Let's set a day.

213
00:16:14.056 --> 00:16:16.058
Otherwise, you may have to wait another year...

214
00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:44.044
Hey?

215
00:16:44.128 --> 00:16:46.755
hello dear Mom is almost home.

216
00:16:46.839 --> 00:16:48.841
Okay, see you later.

217
00:16:55.431 --> 00:16:56.306
To To Hee.

218
00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:03.522
What a scoundrel.

219
00:17:04.023 --> 00:17:06.775
Ruined such a great song, didn't you?

220
00:17:09.778 --> 00:17:10.904
Come on.

221
00:17:38.557 --> 00:17:39.850
Don't like this music.

222
00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:41.727
Why not? I like it.

223
00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.353
I want to dance to something.

224
00:18:00.412 --> 00:18:01.497
Shall we dance?

225
00:18:03.499 --> 00:18:05.167
No, I'm clumsy.

226
00:18:05.793 --> 00:18:07.044
Just listen to me.

227
00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:33.070
When you dance in a couple,
you have to trust your partner.

228
00:19:03.225 --> 00:19:06.353
Now this is our song.

229
00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:31.545
What happened?

230
00:19:32.462 --> 00:19:33.547
What the hell?

231
00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.632
What is it?

232
00:19:35.716 --> 00:19:37.885
I work hard here

233
00:19:37.968 --> 00:19:40.262
and they enjoy themselves all day.

234
00:19:41.763 --> 00:19:43.557
I give up.

235
00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:46.643
It's uncharacteristic of me to work hard.

236
00:19:47.603 --> 00:19:52.357
After all, I'm better at thinking than doing.

237
00:19:52.441 --> 00:19:53.650
That's right. It's time for me to go.

238
00:19:56.695 --> 00:19:58.822
Special meetings of shareholders

239
00:19:58.906 --> 00:20:02.367
for the election of a new chairman, we will be able to
hold on earlier next week.

240
00:20:02.451 --> 00:20:03.535
Spend this week.

241
00:20:03.619 --> 00:20:05.037
It will be difficult.

242
00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.788
A procedure must be followed when…

243
00:20:15.172 --> 00:20:18.425
I pay you an abyss of money,
that you overcome such problems.

244
00:20:18.508 --> 00:20:21.011
Let's accelerate events as much as possible.

245
00:20:28.185 --> 00:20:29.811
As soon as you become the head,

246
00:20:29.895 --> 00:20:34.441
I think your son will head Elektronika Mire.

247
00:20:34.524 --> 00:20:36.777
There's something I've learned

248
00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:39.321
while he was on a run
my mother is over 20 years old.

249
00:20:40.405 --> 00:20:41.865
This is the importance of deprivation.

250
00:20:42.449 --> 00:20:44.868
Deprivation leads to growth.

251
00:20:44.952 --> 00:20:47.829
I plan to teach this son.

252
00:20:50.332 --> 00:20:51.291
Nice shot!

253
00:21:18.402 --> 00:21:19.820
17 YEARS AGO

254
00:21:19.903 --> 00:21:21.822
I'm here, mom.

255
00:21:23.991 --> 00:21:25.075
I have to wash it off.

256
00:21:25.993 --> 00:21:27.077
Yes, I have to.

257
00:21:36.628 --> 00:21:37.713
I have to wash

258
00:21:38.588 --> 00:21:40.007
all your dirty sins.

259
00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:41.258
If I don't wash it...

260
00:21:59.443 --> 00:22:01.903
You know why mom
turned her back on us?

261
00:22:01.987 --> 00:22:05.198
I think she didn't like us.

262
00:22:06.783 --> 00:22:08.243
It was self-hatred.

263
00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:10.996
She despised us
because she despised her own blood.

264
00:22:15.042 --> 00:22:16.918
I think even such a fool as you

265
00:22:18.003 --> 00:22:20.339
must realize that we
at an important crossroads.

266
00:22:22.424 --> 00:22:23.925
We have to convince the public

267
00:22:24.009 --> 00:22:27.596
that we have reliable
and a stable succession plan.

268
00:22:28.305 --> 00:22:29.306
I understand.

269
00:22:29.389 --> 00:22:31.141
I'm not like mom.

270
00:22:31.224 --> 00:22:32.893
I will fix you and use you.

271
00:22:34.311 --> 00:22:37.773
I would never trust that
who is not related to me by blood.

272
00:22:39.107 --> 00:22:40.275
NOTICE

273
00:22:47.199 --> 00:22:48.950
Do you have a second phone?

274
00:22:49.034 --> 00:22:50.035
Just…

275
00:22:51.119 --> 00:22:52.204
It is for girls.

276
00:22:54.039 --> 00:22:55.832
Don't worry. I will fix everything.

277
00:23:04.925 --> 00:23:06.551
EXECUTIVE

278
00:23:09.471 --> 00:23:13.016
{\an8}<i>Why no word from you?
And do not say that you are leaving the game.</i>

279
00:23:20.941 --> 00:23:24.903
THE DEVIL

280
00:23:35.747 --> 00:23:37.916
What a peaceful morning.

281
00:23:40.127 --> 00:23:41.545
It hasn't been for a long time.

282
00:23:42.921 --> 00:23:46.633
In the end, I did
I'm better, Ms. Chu.

283
00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:52.264
I have always believed that happiness is not real.

284
00:24:03.233 --> 00:24:04.484
You got up early.

285
00:24:05.152 --> 00:24:06.361
I have to go to work.

286
00:24:07.279 --> 00:24:08.530
I thought here.

287
00:24:09.322 --> 00:24:11.491
Maybe let's say that yesterday was the eve,

288
00:24:11.575 --> 00:24:13.785
and the anniversary of the company today?

289
00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:17.706
No. Struggling to take a whole year off?

290
00:24:17.789 --> 00:24:20.250
Anniversary deserves though
for two days of celebration.

291
00:24:20.333 --> 00:24:23.003
It seems that you like company less than I do.

292
00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:25.172
Favorite company?

293
00:24:27.757 --> 00:24:29.259
Greetings, Ms. Sin.

294
00:24:29.342 --> 00:24:33.013
<i>Mrs. To, we received
a document from No Suk Min.</i>

295
00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:40.395
You can't sign it.

296
00:24:41.104 --> 00:24:42.480
Everything is already over.

297
00:24:43.732 --> 00:24:45.525
We have to catch the scoundrel
who tried to kill you

298
00:24:45.609 --> 00:24:47.027
find who was behind it

299
00:24:47.110 --> 00:24:49.696
and make sure that he will leave you.

300
00:24:51.114 --> 00:24:52.240
I don't want to

301
00:24:52.324 --> 00:24:53.658
Why not?

302
00:24:53.742 --> 00:24:55.368
I have already fully recovered.

303
00:24:57.204 --> 00:24:59.039
I don't want to start all over again.

304
00:25:00.123 --> 00:25:01.791
I like the peace I have.

305
00:25:03.960 --> 00:25:04.878
WAIVER OF INHERITANCE

306
00:25:04.961 --> 00:25:06.379
{\an8} RECEIVER:
TO TO HI

307
00:25:06.463 --> 00:25:08.381
DIED:
CHU CHONG SUK

308
00:25:17.307 --> 00:25:18.850
What is better for you

309
00:25:20.060 --> 00:25:21.770
became what is best for me.

310
00:25:22.812 --> 00:25:26.691
I decided to leave
that everyone finally finds peace,

311
00:25:26.775 --> 00:25:28.818
and it turned out that I was the one who became happy.

312
00:25:31.279 --> 00:25:33.281
You said that in the world
you have to pay for everything.

313
00:25:33.365 --> 00:25:35.951
Happiness requires sacrifice.

314
00:25:36.534 --> 00:25:38.828
And I think it's worth it.

315
00:25:41.915 --> 00:25:42.999
To To Hee.

316
00:25:46.711 --> 00:25:50.215
Are you really going to give up
without even knowing his face?

317
00:25:51.800 --> 00:25:53.843
If you give up now

318
00:25:53.927 --> 00:25:55.929
then you will live the rest of your life in fear.

319
00:25:56.846 --> 00:26:00.308
You can't keep the peace by covering everything up.

320
00:26:04.145 --> 00:26:05.981
Let's just see his face.

321
00:26:06.690 --> 00:26:07.774
After that

322
00:26:09.276 --> 00:26:10.944
I will do as you say.

323
00:26:17.367 --> 00:26:18.785
OK.

324
00:26:18.868 --> 00:26:21.871
I will see his face
and that's it, okay?

325
00:26:39.556 --> 00:26:41.308
I've been by your side all day.

326
00:26:41.391 --> 00:26:43.018
Why haven't I recharged?

327
00:26:44.394 --> 00:26:46.813
Let's try again when you recharge.

328
00:26:52.485 --> 00:26:54.154
Mr. Choo Seok Hoon has arrived.

329
00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:09.627
Why does Choo Seok Hoon keep coming here?

330
00:27:12.797 --> 00:27:14.466
It's somehow suspicious.

331
00:27:14.549 --> 00:27:15.800
It's just illogical.

332
00:27:16.718 --> 00:27:17.719
What are you talking about?

333
00:27:18.303 --> 00:27:21.181
Mr. Jeon… No, Director Jeon.

334
00:27:21.264 --> 00:27:23.099
He had just survived a deadly attack.

335
00:27:23.183 --> 00:27:25.268
So how could he recover so quickly?

336
00:27:25.352 --> 00:27:27.729
When you say it, something is definitely not right.

337
00:27:28.855 --> 00:27:29.689
show me

338
00:27:30.982 --> 00:27:32.317
Maybe the heavens helped him.

339
00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:33.568
Or ancestors.

340
00:27:33.651 --> 00:27:35.320
You and your superstitions.

341
00:27:43.828 --> 00:27:45.997
Maybe he has a secret.

342
00:27:46.581 --> 00:27:47.707
Secrecy?

343
00:27:47.791 --> 00:27:50.543
Maybe he hides something medicinal.

344
00:27:50.627 --> 00:27:51.544
What?

345
00:27:59.511 --> 00:28:00.512
A mystery, right?

346
00:28:12.565 --> 00:28:13.483
Deliciously.

347
00:28:15.568 --> 00:28:18.196
Since I didn't come
for a meeting and all that,

348
00:28:18.279 --> 00:28:19.948
I wanted to see you.

349
00:28:21.491 --> 00:28:22.409
is everything ok

350
00:28:22.492 --> 00:28:23.326
Yes.

351
00:28:23.410 --> 00:28:26.037
I am much better than I expected.

352
00:28:37.215 --> 00:28:38.216
What a relief.

353
00:28:39.676 --> 00:28:43.430
Do you remember how you used to go with me?
to a tattoo parlor in the USA?

354
00:28:44.681 --> 00:28:46.141
you said

355
00:28:46.224 --> 00:28:49.060
that you are afraid of needles and will never get a tattoo.

356
00:28:49.144 --> 00:28:50.770
I made him drunk.

357
00:28:51.271 --> 00:28:53.356
I didn't even feel anything.

358
00:28:56.985 --> 00:28:58.862
You often behave differently than usual

359
00:28:59.738 --> 00:29:01.948
since I met Mr. Chong.

360
00:29:07.996 --> 00:29:09.080
To Hee

361
00:29:09.914 --> 00:29:11.040
You don't…

362
00:29:13.042 --> 00:29:14.377
do you not regret your decision?

363
00:29:16.212 --> 00:29:18.423
No, I don't regret it.

364
00:29:22.260 --> 00:29:23.470
Thank you Seok Hoon.

365
00:29:25.096 --> 00:29:26.431
And I'm sorry.

366
00:29:36.274 --> 00:29:37.400
Mr. Chong

367
00:29:39.569 --> 00:29:40.528
can we talk

368
00:29:43.740 --> 00:29:45.492
He likes me too much.

369
00:29:51.873 --> 00:29:53.041
{\an8}How are you?

370
00:29:57.462 --> 00:29:58.296
Like new.

371
00:30:00.632 --> 00:30:02.884
You seemed to be in critical condition.

372
00:30:03.718 --> 00:30:05.303
I usually recover quickly.

373
00:30:06.471 --> 00:30:10.266
Vampires stay young
consuming people's blood.

374
00:30:10.850 --> 00:30:13.311
What is your secret?

375
00:30:13.394 --> 00:30:15.772
Delusional about vampires again?

376
00:30:16.314 --> 00:30:18.650
Are you that interested in the occult?

377
00:30:18.733 --> 00:30:20.401
I'm not interested in the occult.

378
00:30:22.946 --> 00:30:24.989
I am interested in you, Mr. Chong.

379
00:30:29.911 --> 00:30:31.871
You're in love with me, right?

380
00:30:32.580 --> 00:30:34.666
Do you like men?

381
00:30:36.668 --> 00:30:37.502
Mr. Chong

382
00:30:38.378 --> 00:30:40.755
What do you get out of a relationship with To Hee?

383
00:30:41.381 --> 00:30:44.384
I don't understand what's the use for you
that you are her husband and protector.

384
00:30:44.467 --> 00:30:45.718
I need her.

385
00:30:48.054 --> 00:30:49.430
If that were true,

386
00:30:50.223 --> 00:30:53.810
you wouldn't sit and watch like her
gives up what is important to her

387
00:30:53.893 --> 00:30:56.145
through you

388
00:30:56.229 --> 00:30:57.856
Finally we are on the same page.

389
00:30:58.731 --> 00:31:00.733
I don't plan to sit and watch.

390
00:31:01.317 --> 00:31:02.360
Satisfied?

391
00:31:04.445 --> 00:31:06.948
The secret of my recovery is a thirst for revenge.

392
00:31:07.031 --> 00:31:09.075
There was no way I could die without paying back

393
00:31:09.158 --> 00:31:10.785
to whoever did this to me.

394
00:31:19.586 --> 00:31:23.089
TO TO HI

395
00:31:26.050 --> 00:31:27.385
Now I am free.

396
00:31:27.927 --> 00:31:29.804
I can finally go out without a bodyguard.

397
00:31:30.638 --> 00:31:31.723
Greetings, madam.

398
00:31:35.894 --> 00:31:38.479
Why don't we have a drink to celebrate?

399
00:31:43.943 --> 00:31:45.820
I forgot how correct you are.

400
00:31:47.822 --> 00:31:48.656
Let's do it.

401
00:31:50.074 --> 00:31:51.284
But one drink at a time.

402
00:31:54.704 --> 00:31:55.622
"MIRE GROUP" WILL ELECT A CHAIRMAN
AT THE SPECIAL MEETING OF SHAREHOLDERS

403
00:31:55.705 --> 00:31:58.124
Looks like Ms. To has officially given up.

404
00:32:02.503 --> 00:32:05.006
I don't think it should end like this.

405
00:32:06.925 --> 00:32:09.427
Something is wrong here.

406
00:32:09.510 --> 00:32:10.511
That's right.

407
00:32:12.347 --> 00:32:13.514
When the speech has already come,

408
00:32:13.598 --> 00:32:16.351
you can draw a photo robot
half of the face?

409
00:32:20.396 --> 00:32:21.606
What do you say?

410
00:32:21.689 --> 00:32:25.193
And you are talented.

411
00:32:25.276 --> 00:32:26.444
More than it seems.

412
00:32:26.527 --> 00:32:28.112
And what do I look like?

413
00:32:28.196 --> 00:32:29.489
Well, look in the mirror.

414
00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:38.039
The game of hide and seek is over.

415
00:32:42.293 --> 00:32:44.462
"SUNVOL FOUNDATION"

416
00:32:50.635 --> 00:32:52.887
The boss works here.

417
00:32:52.971 --> 00:32:56.641
Let's take care of safety and cleanliness here ourselves.

418
00:32:57.433 --> 00:32:58.768
Synchronously!

419
00:33:00.853 --> 00:33:04.816
Make sure the boss
did not inhale a single speck of dust!

420
00:33:14.867 --> 00:33:17.120
- Move!
- Yes, sir!

421
00:33:18.913 --> 00:33:20.039
who are you

422
00:33:20.123 --> 00:33:22.417
- I am the assistant director here.
- Exactly?

423
00:33:23.084 --> 00:33:25.670
Look, the proof is the bags under the eyes.

424
00:33:26.254 --> 00:33:28.089
- Go through!
- Go through!

425
00:33:29.966 --> 00:33:31.009
Director Chon.

426
00:33:31.509 --> 00:33:33.594
You are needed in the theater.

427
00:33:34.637 --> 00:33:37.348
Please drive these dogs out.

428
00:33:42.603 --> 00:33:43.771
The boss has arrived.

429
00:33:47.108 --> 00:33:49.027
Congratulations, boss.

430
00:33:49.110 --> 00:33:50.987
- Congratulations, boss!
- Congratulations, boss!

431
00:33:52.196 --> 00:33:53.990
I said I'm not your boss.

432
00:33:54.615 --> 00:33:56.576
What is illegal work?

433
00:33:56.659 --> 00:34:00.288
A little You all worked so hard.

434
00:34:00.788 --> 00:34:04.125
Please have a drink. Perfectly.

435
00:34:04.792 --> 00:34:06.252
Drive these dogs out.

436
00:34:06.335 --> 00:34:09.130
Performance coming soon. They scare the public.

437
00:34:09.881 --> 00:34:14.469
Thank you very much for your hard work.

438
00:34:15.178 --> 00:34:17.764
You call yourself "Tulkepa",
i.e. "Wild dogs"?

439
00:34:17.847 --> 00:34:19.140
Yes, boss.

440
00:34:19.223 --> 00:34:20.808
- Yes, boss!
- Yes, boss!

441
00:34:22.060 --> 00:34:24.270
Do you know what else your name sounds like?

442
00:34:24.771 --> 00:34:26.814
"Tulkkepa" like sorghum and shallot seeds.

443
00:34:34.739 --> 00:34:35.823
God

444
00:34:36.991 --> 00:34:38.493
You're funny, boss.

445
00:34:38.576 --> 00:34:40.203
Our name, Wild Dogs,

446
00:34:40.286 --> 00:34:44.040
symbolizes our fearlessness and tenacity...

447
00:34:47.001 --> 00:34:49.212
But we will become famous
as the soul of Korean cuisine,

448
00:34:49.295 --> 00:34:51.005
Castor and shallot seeds!

449
00:34:51.089 --> 00:34:55.259
- Castor and shallot seeds!
- Castor and shallot seeds!

450
00:34:55.843 --> 00:34:56.928
Come what may,

451
00:34:58.888 --> 00:35:00.014
I have a task for you.

452
00:35:02.433 --> 00:35:04.018
If you don't do it,

453
00:35:04.102 --> 00:35:08.189
forbid you to appear before my eyes.

454
00:35:08.272 --> 00:35:10.817
We are ready to risk our lives, boss!

455
00:35:11.484 --> 00:35:13.569
- As you say, boss!
- As you say, boss!

456
00:35:19.325 --> 00:35:20.284
Ahead!

457
00:35:20.868 --> 00:35:24.163
- Forward!
- Forward!

458
00:35:36.676 --> 00:35:39.345
Director Jon, it seems
you solved the problem

459
00:35:39.428 --> 00:35:41.305
Are you no longer her bodyguard and husband?

460
00:35:44.684 --> 00:35:46.435
I warned you, didn't I?

461
00:35:47.019 --> 00:35:48.521
after all i said

462
00:35:48.604 --> 00:35:50.773
do you really want to become an insignificant person?

463
00:35:52.108 --> 00:35:54.569
Do you know what it's like to be human?

464
00:35:54.652 --> 00:35:57.321
Every day it seems that you are walking through a thin crisis,

465
00:35:57.822 --> 00:35:59.991
and it seems to give us the right
hunt each other.

466
00:36:00.074 --> 00:36:02.785
People are the most cowardly
and disgusting creatures in the world.

467
00:36:04.954 --> 00:36:07.081
You were perfect because you were a demon.

468
00:36:07.165 --> 00:36:09.750
Death, love, fear...

469
00:36:10.334 --> 00:36:12.170
you were who you were

470
00:36:12.253 --> 00:36:13.713
because he was free from all this.

471
00:36:13.796 --> 00:36:14.755
stop it

472
00:36:14.839 --> 00:36:18.134
There is no way I will back down from To To Hee.

473
00:36:18.217 --> 00:36:19.719
And I will not back down from you.

474
00:36:20.553 --> 00:36:22.847
I won't let you jump
to Gehenna of fire.

475
00:36:23.431 --> 00:36:26.142
This is a final warning, Chin Ka-yeon.

476
00:36:28.269 --> 00:36:29.437
Don't cross the line.

477
00:36:35.318 --> 00:36:37.486
What is so special about it?

478
00:36:37.570 --> 00:36:40.698
Why is it worth it
to risk everything for her?

479
00:36:52.293 --> 00:36:53.586
Star Chin.

480
00:36:54.629 --> 00:36:56.214
how about

481
00:36:56.797 --> 00:36:59.634
to wish them both happiness?

482
00:37:00.218 --> 00:37:02.178
If their happiness comes at too high a price,

483
00:37:03.888 --> 00:37:05.264
this is not true happiness.

484
00:37:24.742 --> 00:37:25.660
Allow me.

485
00:37:26.244 --> 00:37:27.620
No, I will do it.

486
00:37:34.794 --> 00:37:35.628
Cheers.

487
00:37:51.352 --> 00:37:53.771
So nice to drink in the fresh air.

488
00:37:53.854 --> 00:37:55.856
I'm glad you like it.

489
00:37:58.734 --> 00:38:00.820
Finally my journey is complete

490
00:38:01.362 --> 00:38:03.239
although its ending is unexpected.

491
00:38:05.992 --> 00:38:09.120
It was easier to let go
than I thought

492
00:38:10.162 --> 00:38:13.040
So I wonder
why did I hold on so tightly?

493
00:38:13.124 --> 00:38:17.670
Sometimes we put everything on the line
not understanding why they made such a bet.

494
00:38:18.546 --> 00:38:22.842
Maybe we'll find out
only at the end of the trip.

495
00:38:25.177 --> 00:38:27.054
What could be the reason for my trip?

496
00:38:28.681 --> 00:38:29.682
I don't know.

497
00:38:34.478 --> 00:38:35.521
Mrs. Sin.

498
00:38:37.857 --> 00:38:39.317
How was your marriage?

499
00:38:40.026 --> 00:38:42.361
My ex was extremely rude.

500
00:38:43.195 --> 00:38:47.199
I don't know if it is possible
to love and hate a person at the same time

501
00:38:47.283 --> 00:38:49.076
in such a short period of time.

502
00:38:50.202 --> 00:38:53.873
But now that it's over

503
00:38:53.956 --> 00:38:55.416
I understand myself better.

504
00:38:56.500 --> 00:38:58.836
If not for him

505
00:38:58.919 --> 00:39:02.048
I would never understand what I am like in my soul

506
00:39:02.131 --> 00:39:04.133
pathetic, primitive, weak and strong.

507
00:39:04.216 --> 00:39:06.844
This is what my marriage meant to me.

508
00:39:11.390 --> 00:39:15.102
I didn't know you were so passionate.

509
00:39:15.186 --> 00:39:16.562
me too

510
00:39:18.105 --> 00:39:21.108
I have never loved before or after him.

511
00:39:21.192 --> 00:39:24.528
I have been warm all my life,
neither cold nor hot.

512
00:39:25.321 --> 00:39:28.074
But I don't regret it, because it flared up once.

513
00:39:28.699 --> 00:39:31.160
This is probably the reason for your trip.

514
00:39:31.243 --> 00:39:32.078
That's right.

515
00:39:32.870 --> 00:39:35.915
Growth is possible only after destruction.

516
00:39:42.380 --> 00:39:43.214
Cheers.

517
00:39:43.964 --> 00:39:45.174
Well, raise a glass.

518
00:39:47.051 --> 00:39:47.885
To the bottom

519
00:39:56.143 --> 00:39:57.603
She's so crazy

520
00:39:59.105 --> 00:40:01.065
<i>Where are you, man?</i>

521
00:40:02.942 --> 00:40:04.860
To To Hee, your husband…

522
00:40:05.528 --> 00:40:09.323
The train of happiness starts To To Hee!

523
00:40:12.535 --> 00:40:14.328
Ladies and gentlemen.

524
00:40:14.412 --> 00:40:17.498
We are experiencing turbulence.

525
00:40:18.416 --> 00:40:19.542
Turbulence.

526
00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:22.002
Turbulence!

527
00:40:22.753 --> 00:40:24.672
But they are really drunk like dogs.

528
00:40:27.883 --> 00:40:31.011
What is To To Hee?

529
00:40:31.095 --> 00:40:33.889
- Yes, Jon.
- What?

530
00:40:34.473 --> 00:40:35.933
- Yes, Jon.
- What?

531
00:40:36.016 --> 00:40:40.729
I'm sorry that I forced you forever
work late

532
00:40:41.313 --> 00:40:43.107
Nothing.

533
00:40:43.190 --> 00:40:45.401
You pay me just as much.

534
00:40:46.652 --> 00:40:47.987
I think so.

535
00:40:48.571 --> 00:40:50.239
- Here.
- To To Hee!

536
00:40:51.699 --> 00:40:52.950
you better

537
00:40:54.410 --> 00:40:57.621
get together

538
00:41:06.797 --> 00:41:07.631
Hold on.

539
00:41:07.715 --> 00:41:09.550
What is it?

540
00:41:10.134 --> 00:41:11.135
Why do we laugh?

541
00:41:14.388 --> 00:41:15.306
